WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.393
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 9:
Thinking, Feelings, and Imagination.

2
00:00:04.473 --> 00:00:09.300
This unit explores the world inside your
head: thinking, feeling and imagining.

3
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:15.948
You will learn sixteen words for ideas and emotions,
including idea, sense, reason, sadness and experience.

4
00:00:16.028 --> 00:00:23.092
You will practise imagining, making a choice, giving a
reason with because, and suggesting ideas kindly in a group.

5
00:00:23.172 --> 00:00:29.925
In the story The Box of Ideas, children at a school by
the sea fill a special box with their dreams and hopes.

6
00:00:30.005 --> 00:00:35.143
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:35.223 --> 00:00:41.685
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
use abstract nouns like idea, reason, experience,

8
00:00:41.765 --> 00:00:45.026
and sadness to talk about thoughts and feelings.

9
00:00:45.106 --> 00:00:50.176
You will also say what you imagine
and describe the pictures in your mind.

10
00:00:50.256 --> 00:00:54.073
You will also give a reason for something using because.

11
00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.648
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:00:56.728 --> 00:01:02.780
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
idea, imagine, reason, purpose, choice, sense.

13
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:08.513
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

14
00:01:08.593 --> 00:01:15.035
The reading sequence includes The Box of Ideas
at School and Feelings Are Not Bad or Good.

15
00:01:15.115 --> 00:01:20.108
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

16
00:01:20.188 --> 00:01:24.456
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

17
00:01:24.536 --> 00:01:27.277
The first language focus is Abstract Nouns.

18
00:01:27.357 --> 00:01:34.233
An abstract noun names something you cannot see, touch,
or hold, such as a feeling, a quality, or an idea.

19
00:01:34.313 --> 00:01:39.022
Words like idea, experience, sadness
and kindness are all abstract nouns.

20
00:01:39.102 --> 00:01:43.550
They let you talk about what is
happening inside your mind and heart.

21
00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.815
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

22
00:01:47.895 --> 00:01:51.911
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Share an Idea.

23
00:01:51.991 --> 00:01:55.442
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

24
00:01:55.522 --> 00:02:02.646
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

25
00:02:02.726 --> 00:02:04.281
You are ready to begin.

26
00:02:04.361 --> 00:02:11.178
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

27
00:02:11.258 --> 00:02:18.218
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
